    "operations": ["snapshot", "rebuildCurve", "evaluateFraction", "dispose"],
    "construction": "Canonical finite two-point XYZ request; malformed input preserves old edge. Finite geometry resets before inclusive 1e-7 length admission. Actual analytic line trimmed to [0,length], with gp_Dir direction and pinned parameter-bound segment maker.",
    "query": "Clamped finite normalized fraction maps as (last-first)*fraction+first and evaluates the actual edge adaptor; no edge yields undefined. Query failure retires temporary handles and preserves owned edge.",
    "ownership": "Detached request snapshots, reverse-order temporary cleanup, all cleanup attempts despite individual failure, unaccepted edge retirement, independent component disposal. No body or native backend kind/record publication is inferred.",
    "successBoundary": "rebuildCurve boolean means primary curve exists only. Native backend still requires converted-body creation and first-edge admission. This stage does not authorize child midpoint publication or public editor acceptance.",
    "publicBoundary": "Generated worker helper export only; public dispatcher, GUI, MCP catalog/schema and editor operations unchanged."
